🎬 CINEMA TICKET BOOKING SYSTEM (Hibernate MINI PROJECT)
======================================================

📘 PROJECT OVERVIEW
-------------------
The Cinema Ticket Booking System is a console-based Java application built using Hibernate ORM instead of JDBC.

It allows administrators to manage movies and shows.
Customers can view seat availability, book tickets, make payments, and cancel bookings.

The project demonstrates real-time database interaction using Hibernate, covering:
	•	🧩 ORM mapping using JPA annotations
	•	🔗 Entity relationships (One-to-Many, Many-to-One, One-to-One)
	•	🧠 Lazy vs. Eager loading
	•	🧮 HQL queries & Criteria API
	•	💾 Transaction management with Hibernate
	•	🔐 Optimistic locking using @Version
	•	🗃️ First-level & Second-level caching
	•	🧻 Soft deletes instead of physical deletes
	•	🕒 Auto timestamps using @CreationTimestamp & @UpdateTimestamp
------------------------------------------------------

🧩 PROJECT MODULES
-------------------
This project is divided into 3 core modules:

1️⃣ Movies & Shows Management
2️⃣ Seat Booking
3️⃣ Payment & Cancellation
------------------------------------------------------

🎞️ MODULE 1: MOVIES & SHOWS MANAGEMENT
---------------------------------------
🎯 Objective:
Allow the admin to add movies and schedule shows in available auditoriums.

🧱 Hibernate Entities:
	•	Movie
	•	Fields: id, title, language, duration, certification, status, createdAt
	•	Mapping: @Entity, @OneToMany(mappedBy="movie")

	•	Auditorium
	•	Fields: id, name, seatRows, seatCols
	•	Mapping: @Entity

		•	Auditorium_Properties
    	•	Fields: id, screen_type, sound
    	•	Mapping: @Entity

	•	Show
	•	Fields: id, movie, auditorium, showTime, endTime, status

	•	Mapping:
	•	@ManyToOne Movie
	•	@ManyToOne Auditorium
	•	@Version for concurrency

✅ Use Case 1: Add Movie
Admin adds a new movie to the catalog.
Steps:
	1.	Admin enters movie details (title, language, duration, certification).
	2.	Hibernate HQL checks if movie already exists.
	3.	Insert into Movie table via session.persist(movie).

🧠 Hibernate Concepts: JPA Annotations,HQL queries,Persisting entity objects,Soft delete using status field

✅ Use Case 2: Create Show
Admin schedules a new show for a movie.
Steps:
	1.	Select movie & auditorium (Hibernate fetch).
	2.	Enter show date/time.
	3.	Check overlapping shows using HQL.
	4.	Persist show entity.

🧠 Hibernate Concepts: @ManyToOne relationship,HQL time comparisons,Transaction handling

------------------------------------------------------

🪑 MODULE 2: SEAT BOOKING
--------------------------
🎯 Objective:
Allow customers to view seat availability and make ticket bookings.

🧱 Hibernate Entities:
	•	Seat
	•	ShowSeat
	•	Booking
	•	BookingItem

✅ Use Case 1: View Seat Availability
Customer views seats for a particular show.
Steps:
	1.	Enter show_id.
	2.	Fetch all ShowSeat records for that show.
	3.	Display seat map (AVAILABLE/BOOKED).

🧠 Hibernate Concepts: HQL JOIN FETCH,Lazy loading,Mapping entities to console output


✅ Use Case 2: Book Tickets (Atomic Transaction)
Customer books multiple seats at once.
Steps:
1. Select show_id and seats.
2. Check seat availability.
3. Start transaction → lock seats → update to BOOKED → create booking.
4. Commit on success, rollback on failure.
🧠 JDBC Concepts: Transactions, locking, batch updates, GeneratedKeys

------------------------------------------------------

💳 MODULE 3: PAYMENT & CANCELLATION
-----------------------------------
🎯 Objective:
Simulate payment confirmation and allow cancellation before show time.

🧱 Tables:
- payments(id, booking_id, amount, method, status, txn_ref, paid_at)

✅ Use Case 1: Payment Confirmation
Simulate a payment after booking.
Steps:
1. Choose payment method (Cash/Card/UPI).
2. Create payment record with status='SUCCESS'.
3. Update booking status to CONFIRMED.
🧠 JDBC Concepts: UPDATE, transaction consistency

✅ Use Case 2: Cancel Booking
Cancel confirmed bookings before show time.
Steps:
1. Enter booking ID.
2. Validate timing (≥2 hours before show).
3. Start transaction → set booking CANCELLED → free seats → mark REFUND_PENDING.
🧠 JDBC Concepts: Conditional queries, UPDATE, rollback, date comparison

